{
    "background_story": "Malani was a demigod from ancient Polynesian mythology, known for his extraordinary virile strength and bravery. According to legend, he was the son of the great god of the sea and a mortal woman. Malani's physique was chiseled from years of battling fierce storms and wrestling giant sea creatures. His fearless spirit and unwavering confidence inspired his people to stand up against invaders and protect their island home. Malani's most famous exploit was single-handedly defeating a monstrous shark that had been terrorizing the coastal villages. His legendary prowess earned him the respect and admiration of his people, who celebrated his virile strength and unyielding courage in songs and stories for generations to come.",
